Chapter: BoundedNoneLinkedEmpty
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The guard on `__linked-list-empty`'s registry row, and the reason it exists
 is that nothing else in the tree can observe that row. The builtin emits
 `li rd 0` and allocates nothing, so a `bounded none` ceiling over it must
 HOLD. This arm is REFUSED with CDX6101 if the row ever reads anything but
 `none`; it was refused up to 2026-09-07, when the row read `fixed`.

Section: The Declaration That Holds

  bounded none empty-is-free : Integer -> LinkedList Integer
  empty-is-free (n) = __linked-list-empty n

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("empty len: " & show (list-length (__linked-list-to-list (empty-is-free 4))))
  end
